Another observation is that you don't need to sort the array, but you just need to partition it with the value 128. Sorting is n*log(n), whereas partitioning is just linear. Basically it is just one run of the quick sort partitioning step with the pivot chosen to be 128. Unfortunately in C++ there is just nth_element function, which partition by position, not by value.Another observation is that you don't need to sort the array, but you just need to partition it with the value 128. Sorting is n*log(n), whereas partitioning is just linear. Basically it is just one run of the quick sort partitioning step with the pivot chosen to be 128. Unfortunately in C++ there is just nth_element function, which partition by position, not by value.
