This seems to be missing the point of the question, and is answering whether sorting itself is faster with already-sorted arrays. This is less surprising because as this answer points out, there's less work to be done (with most sort algorithms other than merge-sort), on top of the branch-prediction effect. The actual question factors out this effect and is only timing a conditional increment.This seems to be missing the point of the question, and is answering whether sorting itself is faster with already-sorted arrays. This is less surprising because as this answer points out, there's less work to be done (with most sort algorithms other than merge-sort), on top of the branch-prediction effect. The actual question factors out this effect and is only timing a conditional increment.3Reply
